body:
`length` compiles down to `v_sqrt_f32_e32` on my GPU. Square root instructions can be removed by comparing the squared values directly, such as:

```glsl
float min_delta_squared = dot(history - s, history - s);
if (min_delta_squared > dot(history - s1, history - s1)
(...)
```

And so on.

This should improve performance somewhat as the VALU needs to do less work.

Alternatively define a simple `length_squared` function and use that in place of `length`:

```glsl
float length_squared(vec3 vector) {
	return dot(vector, vector);
}
```

